cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Targeted reanalysis of GSE149924: does 15-PGDH inhibition increase autophagy in aged muscle?"
message: "If you use this reanalysis, please cite it and the original study."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "[SURNAME]"
    given-names: "[GIVEN NAME]"
abstract: >-
  Set-level reanalysis of GSE149924 (mouse quadriceps, aged +/- the 15-PGDH inhibitor SW033291),
  using the deposited DESeq2 statistics and an independent re-quantification of the drug contrast
  from raw FASTQs. Finds no transcriptional autophagy-lysosome response, with a working internal
  positive control (respiratory chain) establishing that the comparison can detect coordinated
  low-amplitude shifts.
keywords: [RNA-seq, reanalysis, autophagy, sarcopenia, 15-PGDH, reproducibility]
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    authors: [{family-names: "Palla", given-names: "A. R."}, {family-names: "Blau", given-names: "H. M."}]
    title: "Inhibition of prostaglandin-degrading enzyme 15-PGDH rejuvenates aged muscle mass and strength"
    journal: Science
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1126/science.abc8059
